Sounds like a good idea. Should JavaScript be in charge of creating the elements too? Here's an example:

```javascript
let x = document.createElement("input");
let y = document.createElement("form");
y.appendChild(x);

y.method;          // => "get"
x.name = "method"; // DOM clobbering occurs here
y.method;          // => <input name="method">
```
